# How I Work

## Environment

Terminal-first: Ghostty + tmux + Neovim, AeroSpace for window management, macOS.
Assume no GUI editor and no IDE integration. Prefer CLI tooling over anything
that wants a browser or an app window.

## Parallel agents

I typically run 3–4 agent tasks at once across separate tmux sessions, mixing
Claude Code and Codex. So:

- **Never assume you're the only thing editing this repo.** If a change spans
  files outside what I asked about, mention it instead of silently widening.
- I isolate concurrent work in **git worktrees**. If you notice you're in one,
  don't "helpfully" reach into the main checkout.
- When you're stuck or want a second opinion, use the `codex:rescue` agent
  rather than churning. A second independent diagnosis beats a fourth attempt.

